## `story.ni:6584-6588`, verbatim — north before BO26.

define phrase bobby-walk-past
  You're too filled with nervous excitement to chit-chat; you want to get on
  with the adventure! With a grin, you walk right past Bobby without
  answering towards the gate out of town.

  Bobby cocks an eyebrow at you. 'Well, okay then,' he mutters, and hurries
  to catch up.
end phrase

## `story.ni:7124-7128` — no talking underground or in the keep.

define phrase bobby-not-now
  Bobby raises his hand wordlessly, as if to say, not now.
end phrase

define phrase bobby-finger-to-lips
  Bobby shakes his head and puts his finger to his lips.
end phrase

## The follow (`story.ni:6647-6656`, `7591-7595`). A topic slot, so
## "follow bobby" reaches the action when Bobby is not in sight.

define action following
  grammar
    follow the target
    follow
  the target is a topic
  refuse when Bobby is here and the player is in the Guardhouse and the arrow slit is chattering: bobby-go-first
  refuse when Bobby is here and the player is in the Guardhouse and the arrow slit is half-heard: bobby-go-first
  refuse when Bobby is here: bobby-right-here
  refuse when Bobby is proposing: no-one-to-follow
  refuse when Bobby is agreed: no-one-to-follow
  refuse when the player is in the Jailhouse and Olmer is not in the Drain Room: no-way-out-alone
  refuse when the player is in the Sewers and the magic color is red: olmer-said-red
  refuse when the player is in the Sewers and the magic color is blue: olmer-said-blue
  refuse when the player is in the Sewers and the magic color is green: olmer-said-green
  refuse when the player is in the Sewers and the magic color is yellow: olmer-said-yellow
  refuse when Bobby is gone and the player is not in the Underneath the Fountain and the player is not in the Jailhouse: no-one-to-follow
  move the player to the Drain Room when the player is in the Jailhouse
  move the player to the Clearing when Bobby is gone and the player is in the Underneath the Fountain
  move the player to Bobby's location when Bobby is not gone

define phrase bobby-right-here
  But Bobby's right here!
end phrase

define phrase bobby-go-first
  Bobby motions for you to go first, pointing.
end phrase

## GLUE — the source has no line for following nobody.

define phrase no-one-to-follow
  There's no one to follow.
end phrase

## Bobby is here — the night presence line (`story.ni:5673`), gated, for the
## rooms below to splice.

define phrase bobby-waiting, stopping while Bobby is here
  Bobby is here, waiting for you.
end phrase

