## THE PASTURE (`story.ni:6720-6776`)
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

create the Pasture
  a room
  aka field, open field, pastures, farmland
  north to the Stream Crossing
  northwest is blocked: southern-gate-guarded
  east is blocked: endless-farmland
  northeast is blocked: endless-farmland
  south is blocked: outer-wall-that-way
  southeast is blocked: outer-wall-that-way
  southwest is blocked: outer-wall-that-way

  This wide, open field is used by the city for tourneys and other holiday
  events, or by cattle-sellers driving their livestock to market. Tonight it
  is empty except for the occasional cow pie. To the north you can see the
  dark, rough edge of a forest. {bobby-waiting}

  after the player entering
    first time
      move Bobby to the Stream Crossing
      phrase bobby-fresh-air
      restart the player's dawdle when the player's dawdle has not expired
  end after

define phrase bobby-fresh-air
  You feel nervous and exposed out here in all this empty space; you're more
  used to the narrow alleys and enclosing walls of the city. The urge to
  hunch over and make yourself small is near-irresistible.

  Bobby, meanwhile, strides out into the middle of the moonlit field,
  standing straight and swinging his arms wide. 'Fresh air, Jack!' he calls
  out, laughing. 'Enjoy it! Take a deep breath!' He heads north, still
  laughing.
end phrase

define phrase endless-farmland
  There's nothing out that way but endless farmland.
end phrase

define phrase outer-wall-that-way
  That way lies the outer wall of the city.
end phrase

create the cow pies
  aka cow pie, pie, pies, patty, patties, dung, manure
  scenery, plural
  in the Pasture

  Last time you checked, cow pies pretty much all looked the same.

  when Jack moves, while the player is in the Pasture or the player is in the Stream Crossing
    move the cow pies here
  end when

  on the player smelling
    refuse um-yuck
  end on

  on the player taking
    refuse um-yuck
  end on

define phrase um-yuck
  Um, yuck.
end phrase

define phrase mostly-cow-pies
  Mostly you smell cow pies.
end phrase

